[Chapter "Quieter replies"]
[Line "Hungarian: ...exd4"]
[Opening "Scotch Game: Benima Defense"]

{If Black gives up the centre with ...exd4, take back with the knight.} 1. e4 {Take the centre and open lines for the queen and the f1 bishop.} 1... e5 2. Nf3 {Develop with an attack on e5.} 2... Nc6 3. Bc4 {The Italian: the bishop aims at f7, the weakest square in Black's camp.} 3... Be7 4. d4 {Strike in the centre at once.} 4... exd4 5. Nxd4 {Recapture with a strong central knight. White has more space and easy development.} *
